projects.description:
I had the pleasure of initiating and leading the organization of the "Night of the Right of Asylum" in collaboration with MEDMUN and SciencesPo Refugee Help on March 4, 2021. This significant conference explored the theme of migration at the Franco-Italian border. It focused on reflecting upon the "sheltering" at the Menton Saint Louis Border Police and the respect for rights at the border.

The 10 invited speakers were as follows:

- Philippe de Botton, physician and President of Doctors of the World;
- Raphaël Krafft, journalist and author of "Passeur";
- Martine Landry (activist) and Christine Poupon (asylum issues) from Amnesty International;
- Dominique Simmonot, General Controller of Places of Deprivation of Liberty appointed by French President Emmanuel Macron, and Yanne Pouliquen, controller;
- Zia Oloumi, lawyer;
- David-André Darmon, lawyer;
- Bastien Charaudeau, doctoral student at the School of Law at Sciences Po, currently conducting field research in Briançon for his thesis on the legal processes of marginalization of migrants at the border;
- Emilie Pesselier, coordinator of missions at the internal border at Anafé.

The conference was held in person and livestreamed online for the general public.

The project aimed to inform the general public about the humanitarian situation at the Franco-Italian border. Knowledge will always be the best weapon to uphold human rights worldwide.

To review the Night of the Right of Asylum: https://fb.me/e/3qTIUQm6B

Thanks to Zadig, the campus newspaper of Menton, for their excellent article on our conference. You can find it here: https://issuu.com/lezadig/docs/e_dition_4_final

